      <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      @foreach (var f in faqPairs)
      {
        <h3>@f.Q</h3>
        <p>@f.A</p>
      }

      <h2 id="related">Where to go next</h2>
      <p>Setting the number is half of it. <a href="/guides/collecting-club-subs">Collecting club subs</a> deals with the other half, and its finding is that the payment method matters far less than how often you bill.</p>
      <p>The largest line in the arithmetic above is the hall, and it has more give in it than most clubs realise: <a href="/guides/badminton-court-hire">what UK clubs pay for court hire</a> covers the survey and the levers. The second largest is shuttles, and <a href="/guides/feather-vs-nylon-shuttlecocks">feather vs nylon</a> works out the cost per session.</p>
      <p>If you are setting subs because you are starting from scratch, <a href="/guides/how-to-start-a-badminton-club">how to start a badminton club</a> covers the rest of it.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
        <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px">How this guide was put together</h4>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:0">ePegboard builds club-night software. We do not collect subs, we are not accountants, and we have never set a club's fees. The figures here come from reading 25 UK clubs' published fee pages on 26 August 2026, plus Badminton England's own affiliation prices and the government's published CASC guidance.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0">Three honest limits. The 25 clubs were found through search, not sampled, and the set is England-heavy with one Welsh club and none from Scotland or Northern Ireland. We found no UK benchmark for club reserves, so that section gives a method rather than a figure. And we found no evidence at all on how members react to an increase, so we have described what clubs do structurally and left their reactions alone. Individual Badminton England membership is quoted at more than one price depending on route, and we could not establish which applies to an ordinary club member, so no figure for it appears above.</p>
